Grants and kill switch
Core's level: Permissive · Kill switch: off

Turn the kill switch on?
Everything "Revoke all" ends, and work running now in every pane of this Corbanu Terminal
stops, Claude panes included: a reply in progress is cancelled and its commands are
stopped, as when you interrupt it, and background terminals end.
Until you turn it off here: this Corbanu Terminal sends nothing to the model (each new
turn is refused with a message saying so), messages from other agents wait (Codex panes
get them with their first turn after you turn it off; tasks for Claude panes are sent
when you turn it off), no grant can be issued, protected actions after untrusted content
are refused, the browser and memory writes are refused, and the credential broker stays
closed.
Other Corbanu Terminals running on this home take it too, within about a second: their
running work stops the same way and they refuse new turns.
Saved in security_state.json: it holds after a restart. The level stays Permissive.

